children.translated_text:
) 'What constitutes false speech for us?' The partridge said: 'Speech should be uttered at the proper time, having considered and reflected.' They stopped chattering carelessly and instead spoke only at the proper time, having considered and reflected.
Then they thought: 'We have refrained from false speech, but we have not refrained from the basis of intoxication through liquor, fermented drink, and intoxicants. Let us refrain from the basis of intoxication.' 'What constitutes the basis of intoxication for us?' The partridge said: 'Among fruits, some are intoxicating and some are non-intoxicating. Therefore, from today onward, we should give up intoxicating fruits and consume only non-intoxicating ones.' They gave up intoxicating fruits and began consuming non-intoxicating ones.
Then they thought: 'We observe the five precepts ourselves, but we have not established others in them.' The partridge said: 'Each of us should establish those of our own kind in the five precept-vows.' The monkey said: 'I shall establish all monkeys, wild cats, and other such creatures.' The hare said: 'I shall establish all four-footed creatures such as deer, antelope, and the like.'

